{title: The Whole World Turns In The Palm Of His Hand}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C}
{tempo: 136}

Verse 1
[C7]God [C]bestows wondrous gifts
In the [F]heart of every man.
In His [Em7]image made,
[Em7]By His [D]pardon [F]saved,
In [C]the fullness [C]of His [C]plan.
[C]With a [C]free will [C]to [C]roam,
We [Am7]choose [F]heaven as [F]our [F]home.
[F]He is [G]waiting there
[G]with [Em7]our [F]home prepared
[F]As we journey [C]to [C]His throne.

Chorus
[G]And the whole world turns
In the palm [F]of His hand.
[C]There is beauty in creation,
There is wonder in His [G]plan.
As we walk this earth,
Mountain splendor, oceans grand
[F]All [C]remind [Am]us [A]of our [Em]Maker.
By His Word [F]we understand
[G]That [F]the One to whom [A#]we [G]call
Is Creator of [C]all!
